---
import BytesCorner from "~src/assets/backgrounds/bytes/in-element-corner.svg";

import H from "~src/components/HeadingLink.astro";
import Card from "~src/components/Card.astro";
import BytesSection from "~src/components/BytesSection.astro";
---

<BytesSection color="purple">
  <BytesCorner class="art-bytes-in-element-corner bytes-corner" />

  <H level="2">Frequently asked questions</H>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">How can I use Cellbytes?</H>
      <p>
        Cellbytes can be used by uploading high-resolution images of bone marrow
        aspirates or peripheral blood smears to the platform. The application
        analyzes these images using advanced machine learning algorithms,
        delivering quantitative results and visual annotations. It is accessible
        via a secure web interface&mdash;no installation required.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">Can I test Cellbytes?</H>
      <p>
        Yes, Cellbytes offers a trial version for institutions and professionals
        interested in evaluating its capabilities. You can request trial access
        by <a href="/contact">contacting the support team</a> through the website.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">How robust are the algorithms?</H>
      <p>
        Cellbytes’s algorithms have been trained on a comprehensive real-world
        dataset comprising different pathologies and over 60,000 samples. The
        system achieves high accuracy in detecting and classifying various blood
        cell types and their abnormalities, with performance metrics benchmarked
        against expert diagnoses.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3"> Will Cellbytes replace hematopathologists? </H>
      <p>
        No, Cellbytes is designed to assist hematopathologists. It serves as a
        diagnostic aid that enhances efficiency and consistency. Final clinical
        decisions should always be made by a qualified medical professional.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">Why should I use Cellbytes?</H>
      <p>
        Cellbytes accelerates and enhances hematological analysis by providing
        AI-assisted interpretation of bone marrow and peripheral blood cell
        images. Cellbytes may facilitate remote working and consultation but
        also reduce diagnostic turnaround time and improve standardization,
        particularly in high-volume settings.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">What type of images are supported?</H>
      <p>
        Cellbytes supports high-resolution digital images of May-Gr&uuml;nwald
        Giemsa stained bone marrow aspirate and peripheral blood smear slides.
        Whole-slide images should be captured at 10x magnification and
        region-of-interest images should be acquired at 100x magnification.
        Cellbytes supports multiple imaging formats, such as DZI, SVS, VSI, CZI,
        MRXS, DICOM, and OME-TIFF.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">Why is Cellbytes only cloud-based?</H>
      <p>
        Being cloud-based ensures scalable computing resources and consistent
        algorithm performance across users. Software and algorithm updates can
        be deployed without delays. It also allows for secure data storage and
        easy collaboration between institutes, laboratories and specialists
        across geographic locations.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3"> What is the price of the Cellbytes license? </H>
      <p>
        Pricing depends on your usage volume. Contact the support team to test a
        trial version and discuss your needs. For research use, see the <a
          href="/use-cases/research#pricing-for-research"
        >
          pricing models for research
        </a>.
      </p>
    </Card>
    <Card class="card-item faq">
      <H level="3">Can I use the application for research?</H>
      <p>
        Absolutely. Cellbytes is increasingly used in research settings to study
        hematologic disorders, develop new biomarkers, and support clinical
        trials. It offers data export and integration with other medical data
        domains. Read more about <a href="/use-cases/research">
          how to use Cellbytes for research cases
        </a> and <a href="/publications">
          what research has already utilized Cellbytes
        </a>.
      </p>
    </Card>
  </div>
</BytesSection>

<style>
  .card-grid {
    place-self: center;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--element-padding);
    max-width: 70em;
    z-index: 1;
  }
  .card-item {
    flex: 25rem 1 1;
  }

  .bytes-corner {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: -5%;
    right: -10%;
    height: 100%;

    /* Retint this one instance of the artwork by overriding the token it
       paints with, rather than by overwriting its fills from out here. */
    --bytes-magenta: var(--bytes-light-magenta);
  }

  .faq {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5em;
  }
  /* An odd card left alone on the last row would otherwise stretch to the
     full width and read as a different kind of block than the rest. */
  @media (width > 61em) {
    .faq:last-child {
      max-width: calc(50% - (var(--element-padding) / 2));
    }
  }
</style>
